    {
      "id": "s2018-e2-q02",
      "number": 2,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $u = \\tan x$ is the most appropriate substitution for the integral $\\int \\tan^5 x\\sec^4 x\\,dx$\n\nII. $u = \\sin(2x)$ is the most appropriate substitution for the integral $\\int \\cos^3(2x)\\sin^4(2x)\\,dx$\n\nIII. $\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\cos^2\\theta\\,d\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "I and II only"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "I and III only"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "II and III only"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "All are true"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "None is true"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "D",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L12",
        "L13"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 3,
      "solution": "The official key accepted both C and D for this question. D is stored here because statement I can be defended as true.\n\nII is true. The power of $\\cos(2x)$ is odd, so save one factor $\\cos(2x)$, write $\\cos^2(2x) = 1 - \\sin^2(2x)$, and let $u = \\sin(2x)$, $du = 2\\cos(2x)\\,dx$:\n\n$$\n\\int \\cos^3(2x)\\sin^4(2x)\\,dx = \\frac{1}{2}\\int (1 - u^2)u^4\\,du\n$$\n\nIII is true:\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\cos^2\\theta\\,d\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\theta + \\frac{1}{2}\\sin 2\\theta\\right]_0^{\\pi/2} = \\frac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nI is the disputed statement. With $u = \\tan x$, save $\\sec^2 x\\,dx = du$ and write the other $\\sec^2 x = 1 + \\tan^2 x$:\n\n$$\n\\int \\tan^5 x\\sec^4 x\\,dx = \\int u^5(1 + u^2)\\,du\n$$\n\nBecause the power of $\\tan x$ is odd, $u = \\sec x$ also works, giving $\\int (u^2 - 1)^2u^3\\,du$, a longer polynomial. Both substitutions succeed, so \"most appropriate\" is a judgment call. Reading $u = \\tan x$ as the most appropriate makes all three statements true (D); reading the existence of $u = \\sec x$ as making I false leaves II and III only (C).",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
