    {
      "id": "s2018-e2-q10",
      "number": 10,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "Find the centroid of a thin plate in the shape of the region bounded by $y = \\ln x$, $y = 0$, $x = 1$, and $x = e$. Some of the following results may be useful:\n\n$$\n\\int_1^e \\ln x\\,dx = 1 \\qquad \\int_1^e x\\ln x\\,dx = \\frac{1 + e^2}{4}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\int_1^e x^2\\ln x\\,dx = \\frac{2(1 + e^3)}{9} \\qquad \\int_1^e (\\ln x)^2\\,dx = e - 2\n$$",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\left(\\frac{1 + e^2}{4}, \\frac{e - 2}{2}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\left(\\frac{e - 2}{2}, \\frac{1 + e^2}{4}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\left(\\frac{1 + e^2}{4}, e - 2\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\left(e - 2, \\frac{1 + e^2}{4}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$\\left(\\frac{1 + e^2}{4}, \\frac{2(1 + e^3)}{9}\\right)$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "A",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L9"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 7,
      "solution": "**Note on this question:** The printed hint $\\int_1^e x^2\\ln x\\,dx=\\frac{2(1+e^3)}{9}$ is wrong; integration by parts gives $\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}\\ln x-\\frac{x^3}{9}\\right]_1^e=\\frac{2e^3+1}{9}$. The centroid does not need this integral, and only the wrong choice E uses the printed value, so the answer A is unaffected.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
